  - question: Is heartburn anything to do with the heart?
    answer: >-
      No. It is a burning feeling in the chest caused by stomach acid. But
      chest pain can be a sign of a heart problem, so call 999 if you have
      chest pain that spreads to your arms, jaw or back, or you feel sweaty or
      breathless.
  - question: Can I take reflux medicine long term?
    answer: >-
      Many people do, but your GP should review it regularly and try the
      lowest dose that works. Some people can take it only when needed.
